from lb import e
E=[
e("Book 9 - Summary (John Miller, Yaresh and the messengers)",["Book 9","Yaresh","Battle of Yaresh","John Miller alias","world-taker worms","messenger invasion","Marek defection"],
"""BOOK 9: After the Builder's withdrawal, Rimaros celebrates; Jason's team adopts a second identity: Jason Asano 'leaves with Soramir' while 'John Miller', a silver auxiliary cook, travels with Team Biscuit. Killian Laurent is caught (Havi Estos's tip, Liara's forces); Jason and Hector de Varco fight duels at the royal ball and arena; gold intruders wreck his pagoda; the team departs south by cloud yacht with Carlos's crime wagon, Callum, Arabelle, Amos and Orin Pensinata and Korinne's Team Storm Shredder. They deliver supplies in ruined Cartise (a city torn when the Builder cult stole an astral space), then reach Yaresh, an elf rainforest city threatened by messengers (angelic gestalt beings of astral kings) and a natural array underground. Jason cooks as John Miller, fights in the cage dens (Sophie is the Nightingale champion), meets the valash outworlder Zolit Kreen, the messenger voices Jes Fin Kaal and Fal Vin Garath, kills Pei Vas Kartha (world-taker worm breeder) and frees prisoners. Haliastur the Garuda and Taika (now silver) help against a naga genesis egg. The Battle of Yaresh: Jason projects his soul across the city (Gordon's orrery ritual), Raythe kills diamond messenger Mah Go Schaat, Jason frees Tera Jun Casta from her astral king's mark and Marek Nior Vargas defects with his people to Jason's astral realm. Messengers exist as controlled silver-capped batteries of astral kings.""",9),
e("John Miller (Jason's alias) and the one-star badge",["John Miller","auxiliary adventurer","pentagram stars","Jason alias","second identity"],
"""To stay hidden, Jason keeps a second identity 'John Miller', a silver-rank cook-auxiliary with a one-star Adventure Society badge (star in a circle; cannot take solo missions) while his real three-star identity draws stars as idiosyncratic pentagrams. Vidal Ladiv hands him the paperwork. Jason Asano is said to have left with Soramir; a Shade body stays at the palace as decoy. Team joke: Captain Handsome Boatman, Buck Stone etc. Jason also uses 'Neil Davone' and other aliases in the past.""",9),
e("Killian Laurent captured",["Killian captured","Jaitari","Havi Estos tip","Esteban Galo"],
"""Havi Estos tips Jason that Killian Laurent is in Jaitari (largest city of the Storm Kingdom, central island); Killian kidnaps Havi to bait Jason; Jason had secretly called Liara and Sapphire Crown/Amouz gold-rankers; Killian is chained under a layered ritual array and gives the name Esteban Galo (gold portal user). Cassin Amouz thanks Belinda ('door of House Amouz always open').""",9),
e("The Royal Ball and Duels (Rimaros)",["royal ball","duel Hector de Varco","Lancet de Varco","Draglund","Glenn Twenhey","Smoke Hunter","de Varco","Ileana Irios","Astasia de Varco"],
"""At the palace ball, House de Varco (vehicle makers of Rajoras) challenge Jason's group: Lancet de Varco is withdrawn at the King's request, Hector de Varco (stone-transformation, mimicloth) accepts a four-vs-four set of duels in the old arena under the sky-island lake. Results: Sophie beats Mistress Draglund (Fog of Swords) with Moment of Oneness; Rufus beats Glenn Twenhey with a plain scimitar (counts coup); Humphrey (Immortality) beats the Smoke Hunter; Jason soul-attacks Hector until Soramir stops it. Prize: de Varco vehicle design matrices and materials, which become Jason's cloud yacht (third hybrid mode). Lady Astasia de Varco is gold. Jason: 'I am a republican.'""",9),
e("Jason's yacht and Team Storm Shredder",["Team Storm Shredder","Korinne Pescos","Kalif","Rosa Liselos","Polix","Orin Pensinata","Amos Pensinata","cloud yacht"],
"""Jason's new vessel: a superyacht-sized cloud hovercraft with a bridge piloted by Shade, an owner's cabin and privacy screens (part of his spirit domain; even gods can't see inside). A convoy: Jason's yacht, Carlos's 'Crime Wagon' (prison/hospital/lodging), Callum+Arabelle's skimmer van and Korinne's Outpost Rover. Team Storm Shredder: Korinne Pescos (leader), Kalif (electric chain arrows), Orin Pensinata (silver, Amos's nephew), Rosa Liselos (scout), Polix. Amos Pensinata (gold, might/vast/deep/leviathan; soul-trauma aura like Jason's) trains Jason's aura control (shape rain into ritual circles). Zara (now Zara Nareen, teal hair) joins Korinne's team.""",9),
e("Amos Pensinata",["Amos","Amos Pensinata","There's always work to be done"],
"""Amos Pensinata: gold-rank adventurer (might, vast, deep, leviathan; ocean monsters), gravel voice ('There's always work to be done'); soul-damaged with a Jason-like aura; Carlos met him in a lunatic's dungeon; a favour from Dawn makes him Jason's aura-control mentor if Jason takes nephew Orin. In the Battle of Yaresh he leads a defence. His Greater Miracle Potion cured a burned adventurer.""",9),
e("Melody's backstory and Callum Morse",["Melody backstory","Callum loves Melody","Marta Fries","Sophie's father","Cult of the Reaper handler"],
"""Arabelle reveals Callum Morse loves Melody Jain and was her handler ~25 years. Melody (from an old Order of the Reaper family from Kurdansk) secretly married and had Sophie (Jain) with help from the Church of Fertility; Marta Fries smuggled husband and child away; the Cult of the Reaper ordered Melody to infiltrate Purity's Order of Redeeming Light, where she was 'purified' and lost contact. Sophie was found in a shipwreck near Greenstone, perhaps memory-altered; her father is unknown. Emir's patron (a diamond historian friendly to the cult) had him collect Way of the Reaper books to find her father.""",9),
e("Cartise",["Cartise","Rajoras","Vestine Calhoun","Glorious Harvester","arc lightning lizard"],
"""Cartise: river city destroyed when the Builder cult tore out an astral space and a diamond monster struck; ruins like post-Blitz London; a polished marble-smooth crater; refugees; the lingering magical resonance draws monsters (the Adventure Society wants this to protect refugee towns). Adventure Society guide Vestine Calhoun. Glorious Harvester butterflies (rare swarm monsters) dissolve monster bodies. Rajoras: large southern coastal city on the Rajo estuary, seat of House de Varco. Arc lightning lizards (cobalt iguanas with chain lightning) are the weakest silvers.""",9),
e("Yaresh",["Yaresh","Yaresh elves","elf rainforest city","Urman Vohl","Emresh Vohl","Bellory","Kellance"],
"""Yaresh: elf rainforest city of tens of thousands (glossy black stone walls between giant trees; elves from almond to milk-chocolate skin) on a war footing, with the Church of Knowledge, War's camps and messenger strongholds around and a natural array underground. Underworld: Urman Vohl (entertainment-district boss), sons Valk and Emresh (silver core user who shakes down Bellory). Jason works as cook 'John Miller' at Bellory's pub. Underground fight dens run by Zolit Kreen. Two native diamond elf adventurers, Allayeth and Charist, rule the area.""",9),
e("Zolit Kreen and Benella",["Zolit Kreen","Benella","valash","naga genesis egg","Argrave Mericulato"],
"""Zolit Kreen: valash outworlder (skinny, chihuahua-like heads; Earth humans turned valash by transformation zones), silver fight organiser in a white 80s Miami suit, controlled by his elf aide Benella ('Bennie', ex-adventurer whose team was annihilated; later adopted by Kaal). Zolit is a messenger project: the astral king Vesta Carmis Zell wrapped a NAGA GENESIS EGG (apocalypse beast turning flesh into naga) in his outworlder soul. Argrave Mericulato, a bitter silver functionary, uses a needle to shrink Zolit into the egg orb.""",9),
e("Messengers (Pallimustus)",["messengers","messenger","gestalt beings","astral king messenger","Voice of the Will","Unorthodoxy"],
"""Messengers: gestalt beings (body and soul fused; tall ~1.5x celestine height; wings; alabaster skin, solid gold eyes; no nipples) native to other realities, who believe themselves the highest life of the cosmos; they are the servants of astral kings, whose message is 'Kneel', capped at silver (a seal siphons their potential into the astral king; Voices of the Will can reach gold, diamond messengers may become astral kings). Their bodies/souls give superior aura magic; they use isolation (duel) powers, aura masks, world-taker worms and apocalypse beasts. The Unorthodoxy is dissenting messengers (Marek Nior Vargas) who want to live without astral kings. Resurrection doesn't work on messengers. They are 'budded' like plants (Book 12).""",9),
e("Jes Fin Kaal, Fal Vin Garath and Hess Jor Nasala",["Jes Fin Kaal","Kaal","Fal Vin Garath","Fal","Hess Jor Nasala","Mah Go Schaat","Pei Vas Kartha","Tera Jun Casta","Marek Nior Vargas","Mari Gah Rahnd","Payan Nior Roel"],
"""Yaresh messengers: Jes Fin Kaal (gold, ritualist Voice of the Will, red robe, white wings, serving a female astral king, Vesta Carmis Zell; plots a trap to get Mah Go Schaat killed); Fal Vin Garath (silver, ~8 ft, tests Jason, mouth stripped then restored by Kaal); Hess Jor Nasala (silver, dark skin, silver hair, black-and-white wings); Mah Go Schaat (diamond messenger with brown wings, killed by Raythe); Pei Vas Kartha (lowest-caste silver worm breeder, killed by Jason's Verdict/Colin); Tera Jun Casta (18, 7ft+, pixie cut; duel power; Jason frees her from her astral king's mark); Marek Nior Vargas (gold commander of the breach force, apolitical realist, defects with friend Payan Nior Roel and his people to Jason's astral realm).""",9),
e("World-taker worms",["world-taker worm","apocalypse beast worm","worm town","brood queen","elite worms"],
"""World-taker worms: brown forearm-long chitin-drill-cap parasites classed as apocalypse beasts; take over host bodies and absorb life magic; hosts look alive. Heat-consuming hive-mind; cold is good against them; messengers carry orbs that repel them; elite worms in silver hosts have independent minds. Hidden under a slate-brick workshop: breeding vats, a bloated brood queen and four colour-coded special worms for higher hosts. Colin devours the matriarch and can become a Voice of the Will after hibernation. Carlos finds a way to extract worms if caught early.""",9),
e("Haliastur the Garuda",["Haliastur","Garuda","the Garuda","Little Dawnie"],
"""Haliastur: giant (8+ ft) golden-haired hawk-nosed man with a gourd of amrita and an umbrella, the Garuda (non-essence transcendent presence ~Dawn level), who has chased the naga genesis egg for two decades; knows Shade; mentions Interstice to be introduced after diamond; calls Dawn 'Little Dawnie'. He lets the egg grow and fights a giant diamond-rank hydra of snake heads in garuda form (eagle head, four arms, golden wings, emerald skin).""",9),
e("Taika Williams - Garuda powers",["Taika garuda","Taika silver","Emerald Flesh","King of the Sky","God-Striking Fist","Amrita Taika","Feaster of Serpents"],
"""Taika ranks to silver during the Battle of Yaresh. Garuda confluence (might, swift, bird, wing): Emerald Flesh/Skin, King of the Sky (garuda shape: eagle head, red/gold feathers, talons), Grace of Garuda, Golden Wings, Block Out the Sun, Feaster of Serpents, Amrita, Brother of the Dawn, God-Striking Fist (extreme cost, 666-min cooldown, transcendent at silver), Momentous Charge, Unstoppable Strike, Unbowed aura (Courage boon). Meditation 'Golden Wings Transcending the Heavens'. Beats Fal Vin Garath inside Jason's pyramid bunker. Wants to return to his family on Earth.""",9),
e("Raythe",["Raythe","half-transcendent Raythe","serves the Sand"],
"""Raythe: elf, half-transcendent maximal diamond (amber glowing eyes, light-brown hair with green flecks) who 'serves the Sand' (Keeper of Sands/Moments); accelerates time streams; stops Mah Go Schaat from rushing Jason ('Leave or die... I have time') and kills him, placing the corpse at Jason's feet. Jason drains it with Blood Harvest, gaining a star phoenix availability.""",9),
e("Gordon's orrery ritual and intrinsic-mandate magic",["orrery ritual","intrinsic-mandate magic","soul projection city","aura declaration"],
"""In the Battle of Yaresh Gordon unseals an orrery ritual (intrinsic-mandate magic): a glowing 3D magical orrery that projects Jason's whole soul as a declaration across the entire city, using the Astral Gate (Dawn warned him not to; earlier tapping cost months of convalescence). Messengers' harmonic aura link breaks; about half the silver messengers go berserk or catatonic. Astral kings' magic is intrinsic mandate (their will is law within their domain).""",9),
e("Jason frees Tera Jun Casta; the astral king mark",["soul-shaper mark","astral king mark","messenger seal","Vesta Carmis Zell","Council of Kings","Hallas"],
"""Inside Tera's soul Jason finds (1) a mark ('soul-shaper'; astral king's brand), (2) a sealed potential (messengers capped at silver; Voices' 'raised limits' adjust the seal), (3) the duel power's mechanism (kills both after minutes if neither dies). Jason's own mark translates as 'hegemon' (the language of his sword and Mark of Sin). He overwrites the brand with his own, ends the duel and pops the seal. Vesta Carmis Zell (astral king; soul engineer who watches servant races battle and resurrects them) feels her seal vanish and calls the Council of Kings; her golem servant Hallas is a living soul in a 7-ft white-and-gold body.""",9),
e("Marek's briefing on the natural array",["natural array","subterranean city smoulder","Yaresh array","Marek briefing"],
"""Marek explains the astral king (Vesta Carmis Zell) seeks something buried under Yaresh (why the naga egg was placed there): the natural array, a subterranean city of Smoulder (earth/fire sub-species with centuries of exposure), plus a Builder-cult-occupied astral space below; a three-way war involves Knowledge's army and Adventure Society camps. The array imbues elemental magic and makes messengers mutate with devolving intelligence; essence users and Builder converts resist, so messengers enslave essence users to dig. Kaal wants Jason (an astral king) to lead an essence-user force to retrieve it.""",9),
e("Mercy speech and Jason's moral line",["Jason mercy","soul attack Builder pain","Jason's line","Weight of Sin Pei"],
"""Jason kills Pei Vas Kartha by faith-crushing argument, Verdict and Blood Harvest (star phoenix readiness 0.3%), then nearly tears a cultist's body off his soul (Book 7) and uses a facsimile of the Builder's soul-scouring pain on Tera (which he swore never to use). His father's advice: when someone is at your mercy, it is a chance to decide who you are. 'If no one dares to be a fool, all there will be is darkness.' Shade is his conscience.""",9),
e("Healer visits; Purity's creation; Genesis Command: Life",["Genesis Command Life","Purity sanctioned himself","artefact purge core","Purity relic"],
"""The Healer (brown robes, grey beard) visits Jason in the cloud hospital: Dominion is 'my boy'; sanctioning is an extreme change in a transcendent's nature (the old Builder still exists beneath); Purity sanctioned himself by expending all his authority into an act of creation (an artefact that can purge monster-core effects) that inspired the messenger invasion. The gods unilaterally decree none will interfere in the search; only a new Purity may. Healer gives Jason [Genesis Command: Life] (transcendent legendary, 1 use): gives true life to an astral construct from a dimensional space (bound to that space).""",9),
e("Hana Shavar and the Healer's church in Yaresh",["Hana Shavar","High Priestess Healer Yaresh","Eilaf Hayel","Fiora Luth","Elseth Culie"],
"""Hana Shavar: gold High Priestess of the Church of the Healer in Yaresh (green eyes, light brown hair), runs the refugee camp in Jason's cloud hospital. Eilaf Hayel: gold elf commander of the entertainment-district defence. Fiora Luth: silver Adventure Society logistics admin. Elseth Culie: elf affliction specialist rescued by Jason's Feed me your sins.""",9),
e("Gary leads the craftspeople; Zara's Storm Shredder fights",["Gary Yaresh","forge golem Gary","Gary roar chains hammer","Zara Yaresh"],
"""During the Battle of Yaresh Gary (leonid, almost gold-rank strength; hammer, iron, fire, forge essences; ten-foot six-ton Forge Golem) leads a craftspeople rescue group and defeats a silver summoner messenger; Zara and Team Storm Shredder fight messengers. Rufus's Eclipse zone kills messengers. Onslow's humanoid vessel is speared and his spirit returns later.""",9),
e("Clive's Magister's Ballista and Mana Tide",["Magister's Ballista","Mana Tide","Prismatic Void","Spell Lance Clive"],
"""Clive uses Mana Tide (Balance; 4-hr cooldown; escalating recovery), Wrath of the Magister variants (Prismatic Affliction/Void, Spell & Weapon Enhancement Ritual), Mana Shield, Blood Magic, Vengeance Mirror, Rune Traps, and secretly draws a ritual circle to trigger Magister's Ballista (force spear) killing a messenger. His wand Magister's Tithe was lost; staff Spell Lance of the Magister remains.""",9),
e("Jason vs Tera in the bunker; Emresh Vohl",["Emresh Vohl hides","bunker duel","Tera soul assault"],
"""Jason (in heart-print boxers) fights Tera Jun Casta in an isolation sphere, then through a breach into the entertainment-district bunker warehouse. His astral realm/soul can't be suppressed by her soul-shell. Emresh Vohl hiding as a civilian recognises 'the tavern man'. Jason overwrites her mark and she remains unconscious weeks after.""",9),
e("Book 9 aftermath: Marek's people, Cloud flask maker, Rick's team",["cloud flask maker","Marek asylum","Pios Val Haat","Rick Geller Yaresh","Allayeth","Charist"],
"""Weeks after the battle: city rebuilding; Jason hides in his soul space dodging diamond-rankers (who broke into his cloud palace; Hana filed complaints). The cloud flask's maker, a nondescript gender-shifting diamond-ranker woman, waits outside; her override device can return Emir's palace to its flask but not Jason's. Marek's people accept Jason as an astral king: he swaps their astral-king marks for their own marks (Pios Val Haat refuses and dies). Rick Geller's team (Hannah, Claire, Phoebe, Dustin Kettering) arrives as 'translators'; Allayeth and Charist (diamond elf adventurers) are frustrated; Soramir says force is a bad idea.""",9),
e("Emir's treasure hunt at Yaresh",["Emir treasure hunt","Isart","Purity cleansing artefact hunt","diamond community artefact"],
"""Emir Bahadir (with Constance, now gold and his wife) is hired by diamond-rank clients to find the artefact that cleanses monster-core effects (Purity's creation), as one of many middlemen; adventurers aren't told the target. Messengers seek a monopoly on turning core users into non-core users. Humphrey decides Team Biscuit will participate but not hand it over blindly.""",9),
e("Jason's soul-space upgrades (Book 9)",["Colin storehouse","dark jungle greenhouse","astral estate","Colin Voice of the Will"],
"""Jason builds a dark jungle greenhouse (black red-sheen brick, pit of blood) as Colin's biomass storehouse; Colin and Gordon accepted a crude permanent bond via the astral throne/gate while Jason was unconscious (astral kings bestow powers through bonds). Colin can become a Voice of the Will after hibernation in the astral kingdom. Jason promises Gordon an upgrade; Shade isn't linked the same way.""",9),
e("Jason's Silver 4 and abilities list (Book 9)",["Verdict silver 4","Blood Harvest star phoenix","star phoenix readiness","Jason silver 4"],
"""Jason's abilities silver 4: Verdict (S4, transcendent, Sanction), Blood Harvest (can move toward star phoenix state readiness by absorbing diamond corpses), Feast of Absolution (revokes afflictions leaving transcendent damage on messengers), Sin Eater raises maxima. His eyes have nebula irises and void-black sclera; Belinda gives him a pair of blue coins (appearance device restoring dark brown human eyes). Jason's hood shows a head silhouette; his cloak looks like a portal.""",9),
]
